WOWII-103 MOTIF = INFLATION/DECOUPLING: a small CORE + pendant LEAVES that pump ONE
invariant (independence 9) while a coupled invariant (ecc, bipartite) stays fixed,
breaking a conjectured inequality alpha <= 8. Found by exhaustive 2^11 search + Lean.

THE REPO ALREADY USES THIS MOTIF. Check: the LRC extremal {1..11,13,24} is a
LEAF-INFLATION of the base family {1..13} -- swap the 'core' speed 12 for a SACRIFICIAL
pendant 24 = 2*12 that reproduces the same danger comb at t*=1/14 but is a 'leaf'.
  {1..13} base             M=1/14   (=1/14 tight)
  {1..11,13,24} inflated   M=1/14   (=1/14 tight)
  {1..11,13,36} gap        M=3/41   (0.07317073170731707)
  => {1..11,13,24}: replace 12 by 24 (a '2x leaf'); SAME M=1/14 at t*=1/14 because
     24*(1/14)=12/7, ||12/7||=||-2/7||... the leaf reproduces the core's danger. This is
     EXACTLY the WOWII pendant-inflation: a leaf that pumps the config without changing
     the binding invariant. (The (1/14,3/41) gap family {1..11,13,36} is another leaf.)

THE DECOUPLING VIEW (THM-1820 is the repo's own WOWII). WOWII-103 breaks a conjectured
COUPLING of independence to eccentricity; THM-1820 broke the conjectured coupling of
H-maximal to 3-cycle-maximal (they are DECOUPLED, opposite strata). SAME phenomenon:
a conjectured inequality between two invariants dies to a construction that decouples
them. So the transferable rule: to break an invariant-inequality, DECOUPLE via inflation.

TRANSFERABLE METHOD (WOWII -> repo):
  1. INFLATION: small core + sacrificial 'leaf' (LRC: 2x speed; JC: append identity
     coordinate; tournament: dominated/dominating vertex) pumps one invariant.
  2. EXHAUSTIVE small-case certification (repo already does; e.g. 59048 nullcone sweep).
  3. LEAN certification of the finite invariants (repo has TournamentH7) -- the WOWII PR
     Lean-certified alpha=9,b=10,ecc=30/11 by decide+native. The repo could Lean-certify
     its extremal LRC/tournament invariants the same way.
